  "title": "Eastern Orthodox Christianity",
  "summary": "The history of Constantinople as a patriarchate began in 330, when Constantine I moved his government to Byzantium. From 520 its head became known as the ecumenical patriarch. After the 11th-century schism with Rome, the patriarch became first among equals of the Orthodox churches. The Byzantine Empire lasted until 1453. Over the last century the Orthodox population has more than doubled to nearly 260 million, with its centre in Central and Eastern Europe and a growing community in Ethiopia.",
